hadiths[54]{hadithnumber,text}:
"794","Sayyiduna Alqamah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I used to go with Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) in Mina when Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) met Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him), and they stood and began talking. Then Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: O Abu Abdur Rahman! Should we not arrange your marriage with a young girl so that she may remind you of some of your past days? So Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: If you say this, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to us: O group of young men! Whoever among you has the means to marry should marry, for it lowers the gaze and protects the private parts (from adultery and the like), and whoever is not able to do so should fast, for it will be a protection for him, as if castrating himself."
"795","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that some companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked the wives of the Prophet (may Allah be pleased with them) about the secret worship of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (i.e., the worship he performed at home). Then one of them said, ""I will never marry women."" Another said, ""I will never eat meat."" Another said, ""I will never sleep on a bed."" (When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was informed of this,) the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praised and glorified Allah and said, ""What is the matter with people who say such and such things? (As for me, during the night) I pray and I sleep, I fast and I break my fast, and I marry women. So whoever turns away from my way is not from my Ummah."""
"796","The conqueror of Persia, Sayyiduna Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When 'Uthman bin Maz'un (may Allah be pleased with him) intended to abstain from women, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade him. And if the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had permitted him, then we (all) would have become eunuchs."
"797","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The goods of this world are things for use, and the best thing for use in this world is a righteous woman."
"798","Narrated by Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: A woman is married for four reasons: for her wealth, for her lineage, for her beauty, and for her religion. So attain success by marrying the religious one, may your hands be dusted."
"799","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that Sayyiduna Abdullah (the father of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him) passed away and left behind nine or seven daughters (the narrator is unsure). So I married a previously married woman (one who was divorced or whose husband had died). The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said to me, ""O Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), have you married?"" I replied, ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah!"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, ""To a virgin or a previously married woman?"" I replied, ""O Messenger of Allah! To a previously married woman."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Why did you not marry a virgin, so that she could play with you and you could play with her, or (he peace and blessings be upon him) said, so that she could joke with you and you could joke with her?"" Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""I replied, 'My father Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) passed away and left behind nine or seven daughters, and I did not think it appropriate to bring a girl like them (i.e., a young girl) among them. I thought it better to bring a wife (into my marriage and for their upbringing) who would look after them and reform them.'"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""May Allah bless you,"" or he said some other good words."
"800","'It is narrated from Abdur Rahman bin Shumasa that he heard Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) while he was saying on the pulpit: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: A believer is the brother of a believer. So it is not permissible for any believer to sell over the sale of his brother, nor is it permissible for him to propose (marriage) over the proposal of his brother, until he leaves it.'"
"801","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: I have married a woman from among the Ansar. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: Did you look at her? For indeed, there is something (a defect) in the eyes of the Ansar. He replied: Yes, I have seen her. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: For how much mahr (dowry)? He said: For four uqiyah of silver. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Four uqiyah? It is as if you people dig up silver from the side of this mountain (i.e., when you fix such a large mahr), and we have nothing to give you. But now, we will send you with an army, and you will get a share (of the spoils of war) in it. The narrator says: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sent an army towards the tribe of Banu Abs, and he sent him along with it."
"802","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: A widow should not be married until her permission is sought, nor should a virgin be married until her permission is sought. The people asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! How is the permission of a virgin taken?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Her permission is her silence."
"803","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: A widow has more right regarding her marriage than her guardian, and a virgin should be asked for permission regarding her marriage. And her permission is her silence."
"804","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Of all conditions, the most deserving to be fulfilled are those conditions by which you have made private parts lawful for yourselves, that is, the conditions of marriage."
"805","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) married me when I was six years old, and when I was sent to his house (rukhsati), I was nine years old. She says: Then we came to Medina, and there I had a fever for a month, and my hair reached my ears (i.e., it had fallen out during the illness). Then Umm Ruman (she is the mother of Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her) came to me while I was on a swing, and my friends were with me. She called me, so I went to her, and I did not know why she had called me. Then she took my hand and made me stand at the door, and I was gasping (as someone does when out of breath) until my breathing calmed down. She took me into a house where there were some women of the Ansar, and they said: May Allah bless you and grant you a share of goodness. (In short) my mother handed me over to them. They washed my head and adorned me, and I did not feel any fear until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came at forenoon and I was handed over to him."
"806","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came to Khaybar during the expedition, and we performed the morning prayer near Khaybar in darkness. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) mounted (his ride), and Sayyiduna Abu Talha (may Allah be pleased with him) also mounted, and I was riding behind Abu Talha (may Allah be pleased with him). The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) entered Khaybar on his mount, and my knee was touching the thigh of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) (because) the cloth had slipped from the thigh of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and I was seeing the whiteness of his thigh. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) entered the settlement (Khaybar), he proclaimed, “Allahu Akbar! Khaybar is destroyed,” meaning Allah is the Greatest and Khaybar is ruined. And he said, “When we descend in the courtyard (field) of a people (then the morning of those who were warned of Allah’s punishment is an evil one).” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) proclaimed this three times. Sayyiduna Anas said that the people (the Jews) were going about their work. (When they saw the army and heard the voice of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)), they said, “By Allah, Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) has arrived with his army.” Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that we conquered Khaybar by force and the captives were gathered in one place. Then Sayyiduna Dihyah Kalbi (may Allah be pleased with him) came and said, “O Messenger of Allah! Give me a slave woman from among the captives.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Go and take any slave woman you wish.” He chose Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) (who was among the captives) and took her. Then a man came to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, “O Messenger of Allah, you have given Dihyah (may Allah be pleased with him) Safiyyah bint Huyayy, who is the daughter of the chief of Banu Qurayzah and Banu Nadir; she is only suitable for you.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Call Dihyah (may Allah be pleased with him) and that slave woman.” They brought Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her). When the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) saw Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her), he said (to Dihyah (may Allah be pleased with him)), “Take any other slave woman besides Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her).” Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) freed Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) and married her. Thabit asked Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), “O Abu Hamzah, how much did the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) give her as mahr (dowry)?” Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) replied, “Her mahr was her own self, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) freed her and married her (this freedom was her mahr).” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was still on the journey when Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) adorned and prepared Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) and brought her to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). In the morning, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was in the state of a bridegroom. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Whoever has any food, let him bring it.” And the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) spread a cloth, so someone brought cheese, someone brought dates, and someone brought ghee. The Companions mixed all these things and made hasees (a dish) and ate it. This was the wedding feast (walimah) of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"807","Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever frees his slave woman and then marries her, he will have a double reward."
"808","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade Shighar marriage. And Shighar was that a man would marry his daughter to another on the condition that the other would also marry his daughter to him, and no dowry would be fixed between them."
"809","Qais said: I heard Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) say: We used to participate in jihad with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and we had no women with us, so we said, ""Should we not castrate ourselves?"" But the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade us from doing so. Then he permitted us to contract marriage with a woman for a specified period in exchange for a garment (i.e., temporary marriage, mut'ah). Then Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) recited this verse: ""O you who believe! Do not make unlawful the good things which Allah has made lawful for you, and do not transgress. Verily, Allah does not love the transgressors."" (Al-Ma'idah: 87)"
"810","Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We used to contract temporary marriage (mut'ah) during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) by giving a handful of dates and flour (as dowry) to women for several days, until Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) forbade it in the case of Amr bin Harith."
"811","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade temporary marriage with women and eating the meat of domestic donkeys. (That is, wild donkey is not forbidden.)"
"812","It is narrated from Rabi’ bin Sabrah that his father (may Allah be pleased with him) was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in the expedition of the conquest of Makkah, and he said: We stayed in Makkah for fifteen (i.e., thirty days including nights and days), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) permitted us to contract mut’ah with women. So I and a man from my tribe both went out, and I was more handsome than him, and he was closer to being unattractive. Each of us had a cloak, and my cloak was old, while my cousin’s cloak was new and fresh. When we reached the lower or upper side of Makkah, we met a woman who was like a young she-camel, with a long neck (i.e., a young, beautiful woman). So we said to her: Do you wish that one of us contracts mut’ah with you? She said: What will you give? So each of us spread out his cloak, and she began to look at both of them. My companion was staring at her (from her head to her hips), and she said: His cloak is old, and my cloak is new and fresh. Then she said two or three times: There is no harm in his cloak. So I contracted mut’ah with her. Then I did not leave her until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) made mut’ah unlawful."
"813","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Sabrah Juhani, may Allah be pleased with him, that he was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him. The Prophet said: ""O people! I had permitted you to contract temporary marriage (mut'ah) with women, but now Allah Almighty has made it unlawful until the Day of Resurrection. So, whoever has any of these women (i.e., women of mut'ah) with him should let her go, and do not take back anything you have given them."""
"814","It is narrated from Nabiya bin Wahb that Umar bin Ubaidullah intended to marry his son Talha bin Umar to the daughter of Shaiba bin Jubair. So he sent a messenger to Aban bin Uthman, who was the Amir of Hajj at that time, so that he would also come (at the time of the marriage). So Aban came and said that I heard Sayyiduna Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: A Muhrim (one who has entered the state of Ihram for Hajj or Umrah) should neither marry himself, nor arrange the marriage of another, nor propose for marriage."
"815","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) who says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) married Umm al-Mu'mineen Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) while he was in the state of Ihram (i.e., in the sacred state)."
"816","Sayyiduna Yazid bin Asam رضي الله عنه says that Umm al-Mu'mineen Maymunah bint al-Harith رضي الله عنها herself narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم married her while he was in a state of being halal (not in ihram), and Maymunah رضي الله عنها was the maternal aunt of both myself and Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما."
"817","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade marrying four women together, and they are: a woman and her paternal aunt, and a woman and her maternal aunt."
"818","Abu Salamah bin Abdur Rahman narrates: I asked Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), ""What was the dowry of the wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)?"" She replied, ""The dowry of the wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was twelve uqiyah and one nash."" (She) asked, ""Do you know the amount of a nash?"" Abu Salamah says, ""I said, I do not know."" She said, ""It is half an uqiyah. This totals five hundred dirhams, and this was the dowry of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) for his wives."""
"819","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a trace of yellow color on Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him), so he said: ""What is this?"" He replied, ""O Messenger of Allah! I have married a woman for a dowry of a date stone's weight of gold."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""May Allah bless you. Give a wedding feast, even if it is with only one goat."""
"820","Sahl bin Sa’d Sa’idi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, “O Messenger of Allah! I have come to offer myself to you (as a wife).” (This refers to the verse: “If a believing woman offers herself to the Prophet, and the Prophet wishes to marry her, this is only for you and not for the (rest of) believers.” And from this, the permissibility of such a gift is established only for the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). (Al-Ahzab: 50)) Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) looked at her from top to bottom and then lowered his blessed head. When the woman saw that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had not made any decision regarding her, she sat down. Then a companion stood up and said, “O Messenger of Allah! If you have no need of her, then marry her to me.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Do you have anything (to give as a dowry)?” He replied, “O Messenger of Allah! By Allah, I have nothing.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Go to your family and see if you can find something.” He went and returned and said, “By Allah, I found nothing.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said again, “Go and look, even if it is an iron ring.” He went and returned and said, “By Allah, O Messenger of Allah! Not even an iron ring, but this is my lower garment, I will give half of it to her.” The narrator, Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him), said that the poor man did not even have an upper garment. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “What will she do with your lower garment? If you wear it, she will have nothing of it, and if she wears it, you will have nothing of it.” Then that man (disappointed) sat down, and after sitting for a long time, he stood up. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saw him turning away, he ordered him to be called. When he came, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Do you know any part of the Qur’an?” He said, “I know such and such surahs,” and he counted them. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, “Can you recite them by heart?” He replied, “Yes.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Go, I have married her to you in exchange for the Qur’an you know (i.e., teach her these surahs, this will be your dowry).”"
"821","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I used to feel great jealousy towards those women who would offer themselves to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). And I used to say: How does a woman offer herself? Then when this verse was revealed: “O Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)! You may put off whom you please of them, and you may take to yourself whom you please, and whom you desire of those whom you had set aside, there is no blame on you” __QUR_N__, I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): By Allah, I see that your Lord hastens to fulfill your desires."
"822","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) married me in the month of Shawwal and my wedding was also in the month of Shawwal, and which woman was dearer to the Messenger of Allah than me? And Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) liked that the women of her tribe should also have their weddings in the month of Shawwal."
"823","Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not give a better and more generous wedding feast (walima) on the occasion of marrying any of his wives than he did for Umm al-Mu'mineen Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her). So Thabit Banani asked, ""What did he (peace and blessings be upon him) serve at the walima?"" He replied, ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) served meat and bread, until the people ate to their fill and food was left over."""
"824","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) got married and entered upon his purified wife (may Allah be pleased with her), and my mother Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) made some hais and placed it in a dish and said, “O Anas! Take this to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).” (From this it is proven that sending food to the new groom to help with the walima is recommended.) “And say that my mother has sent this especially for you in your service, and she sends her greetings, and she says: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! This is a very small gift from us in your service.” Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Then I took it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I said, “My mother has sent me to you and sends her greetings, and she says: This is a very small gift from us in your service.” So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Put it down and go call so-and-so and so-and-so to us, and whoever you meet,” and he mentioned several people by name. So I brought those whom he named and also those whom I met. The narrator says: I asked Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), “How many people were there in total?” He said, “About three hundred.” And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me, “O Anas! Bring that dish.” Then those people came in until the Suffah, the platform, and the room were filled. (The Suffah is the place made for sitting outside, which is called the guest room.) Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Let ten people sit in a circle at a time (i.e., when they finish eating, then another ten should sit), and each person should eat from what is near him (i.e., do not break the top of the food, for the blessing descends from there).” Then they ate until all were satisfied, and one group would eat and leave, then another would come, until all had eaten. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me, “Anas, pick up this (dish),” and when I picked it up, it was not clear whether there was more food in it when I put it down or when I picked it up. And some people sat in the house of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and began talking, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting, and his purified wife (i.e., Umm al-Mu’minin Zaynab, may Allah be pleased with her) was sitting with her face turned toward the wall. Their sitting was burdensome to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he went out and greeted all his purified wives (may Allah be pleased with them) and then returned. When those people saw that they were being a burden to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they quickly went to the door and all went out. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and put up a curtain and entered inside, and I was sitting in the room. After a short while, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to me, and these verses had been revealed to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and recited to the people: “O you who believe! Do not enter the houses of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) unless permission is given to you for a meal, not (so early as) to wait for its preparation. But when you are invited, enter; and when you have eaten, disperse, without seeking to remain for conversation. Such (behavior) annoys the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he is shy of (asking) you (to go); but Allah is not shy of (telling you) the truth...” to the end of the verse. (Al-Ahzab: 53). (The narrator of the hadith) Ja’d said that Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: “I was the first to hear and receive these verses, and the wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to observe the veil.”"
"825","Narrated from Nafi that Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) used to narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that when someone invites his brother, he should accept his invitation, whether it is a wedding invitation or any other similar invitation."
"826","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When someone is invited, he should accept it; if he is fasting, he should pray (for the host), and if he is not fasting, he should eat."
"827","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The worst food is the food of a wedding feast in which those who wish to come are prevented, and those who do not wish to come are invited. And whoever does not accept the invitation has disobeyed Allah the Exalted and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"828","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If any of you, at the time of intending intercourse, says ""Bismillah... ma razaqtana"" then if Allah has decreed a child for them, Satan will not harm him. And its meaning is: I begin with the name of Allah; O Allah! Protect us from Satan and keep Satan away from the offspring You grant us."
"829","Ibn al-Munkadir narrates that he heard from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Jews used to say that if a man has intercourse with his wife from behind (but in the vagina), then the child born will be cross-eyed (i.e., sees one thing as two). Upon this, the verse was revealed: ""Your wives are a place of sowing of seed for you, so come to your place of cultivation however you wish"" (Al-Baqarah: 223). (Meaning: come to the place of cultivation and not to the well, and the place of cultivation is only that where the seed is sown and grows, not the place where the seed is wasted.)"
"830","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man calls his wife to his bed and she does not come, and the man remains angry with her throughout the night, then the angels continue to curse her until morning."
"831","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The worst person in the sight of Allah on the Day of Resurrection is the one who goes to his wife and she comes to him (i.e., they have intercourse), and then he discloses her secret."
"832","´Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""All of my Ummah will be forgiven except those who disclose (their sins), and disclosing is that a person commits a (bad) deed at night, and when morning comes, Allah has concealed that (bad deed), but he himself says, 'O so-and-so! Last night I did such-and-such (bad) deed,' even though he committed the bad deed at night (and) Allah had concealed it. At night, the Lord conceals, and in the morning, this (person) removes Allah's covering."""
"833","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the mention of 'azl (withdrawal) was made in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Why do you do this?"" The companions said: ""Sometimes a man has a woman who is breastfeeding a child, he has relations with her and dislikes that she becomes pregnant, and sometimes someone has a slave woman, he has relations with her and does not want her to become pregnant."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not do this, for pregnancy or non-pregnancy is by decree."" Ibn 'Awn said: ""I narrated this hadith to Hasan, so he said: 'By Allah, there is a reprimand (scolding) in this for practicing 'azl.'"""
"834","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), he states that a man asked the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), ""I have a slave woman with whom I practice coitus interruptus (withdrawal)."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""If Allah intends to create someone, this (withdrawal) cannot prevent it."" (A few days later) that man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""The slave woman I mentioned to you has become pregnant."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger."""
"835","‘Sayyidah Judamah bint Wahb Asadiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her), the sister of Sayyiduna ‘Ukkashah, says: I went with some people to the service of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he was saying: I intended to prohibit ghīlah, but then I saw that the people of Rome and Persia practice ghīlah and it does not harm their children. Then the Companions asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about ‘azl (withdrawal), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: It is a hidden “wa’d” (i.e., it is secretly burying the child alive)."
"836","Sayyiduna Abu Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he passed by the door of a tent and saw a woman there whose time of childbirth was near. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Perhaps the man (with whom she is) intends to have intercourse with her?” The people replied, “Yes.” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “I wished to curse him with such a curse that would remain with him till the grave. How can he be the heir of that boy, when she is not lawful for him? And how can he make that boy a slave, when he is not lawful for him?”"
"837","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an army towards Autas on the day of Hunain. They confronted the enemy, fought them, prevailed over them, and captured their women. Some of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked having relations with them because their husbands, who were polytheists, were still alive. Then Allah the Exalted revealed this verse: ""Forbidden are women who are married, except those whom your right hands possess"" (An-Nisa: 24), meaning that when their waiting period ('iddah) has passed, they are lawful for you."
"838","´Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) had nine wives, and when he would take turns among them, he would come to the first wife on the ninth day. (For this reason) it was the custom of the wives that whichever house the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was in, they would all gather in that house. One day, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was in the house of Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her), and Umm al-Mu’minin Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her) came, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) reached out his hand towards her. So (Aisha) said, ""This is Zainab."" Thus, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) withdrew his hand, and a dispute began between Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa and Zainab (may Allah be pleased with them both), until their voices were raised and the call to prayer was made. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) passed by them and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Go out for the prayer and put dust in their mouths."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went out, and Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said, ""Now when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) has finished the prayer, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) will come and be angry with me."" Then, when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had finished the prayer, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) came to them and scolded them harshly and said, ""Do you do such a thing (i.e., do you shout and raise your voice in front of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him)?"""
"839","Narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) married her, he stayed with her for three days and then said: ""You are not insignificant to your husband. If you wish, I will stay with you for a week, and if I stay with you for a week, then I will stay with each of my other wives for a week (and then after all of them, your turn will come again)."""
"840","`Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` when (a man) marries a virgin and he already has a previously married woman in his marriage, then he should stay with the virgin for seven days (and after that, he should assign turns). And when he marries a previously married woman while he already has a virgin, then he should stay with her for three days. Khalid (the narrator of the hadith) said: If I say that this narration is marfu‘ (attributed to the Prophet), then that would also be true, but Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) used these words and said: This is the Sunnah."
"841","‘Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I did not see any woman whom I wished to be in her body more than Saudah (may Allah be pleased with her); she was a quick-tempered woman. Then when she became old, she gave her turn to Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) and said: O Messenger of Allah! I have given my turn to Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would stay with Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) for two days, one for her own turn and one for the turn of Saudah (may Allah be pleased with her)."
"842","‘Ata says: We attended the funeral of Umm al-Mu’minin Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) at Sarf with Sayyiduna Ibn ‘Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both). Sayyiduna Ibn ‘Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: Be mindful that she is the purified wife of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). When you lift her blessed bier, do not shake or jostle it, and carry it with great gentleness. And that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had nine purified wives, of whom eight had an assigned turn and one did not. ‘Ata said: The one for whom there was no assigned turn was Umm al-Mu’minin Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her). (This is the narrator’s error; the correct view is that Umm al-Mu’minin Sawdah (may Allah be pleased with her) gifted her turn to Umm al-Mu’minin ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), as mentioned in the narration above.)"
"843","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) saw a strange woman. He (peace and blessings be upon him) came to Umm al-Mu'mineen Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her) and she was rubbing leather (to dye it) at that time. He (peace and blessings be upon him) fulfilled his need (sexual intercourse) and then came out and said: Verily, a woman comes in the form of Satan and goes in the form of Satan. (That is, seeing her arouses satanic thoughts.) So when any of you sees (a strange) woman (and satanic thoughts arise), he should go to his wife; by this action, the corrupt thoughts in his heart will go away."
"844","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, it is necessary for him that when any matter arises, he should speak good or remain silent. And treat women well, for they were created from a rib, and the most crooked part of the rib is its uppermost part. If you try to straighten it, you will break it, and if you leave it as it is, it will remain crooked. So treat women well."
"845","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No believing man should harbor intense aversion towards a believing woman; if he dislikes one of her habits, he will surely be pleased with another. Or he said something similar using the word ""ghairah."""
"846","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If it were not for the Children of Israel, food and meat would never decay. And if it were not for Hawwa (Eve), no woman would ever betray her husband."
"847","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): We were on a campaign with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). When we were returning, I was urging my camel, which was very slow, to move quickly. Then a rider came from behind and struck my camel with a stick he had, and my camel started moving as if it were a very good camel. I looked back and saw that it was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He said, ""O Jabir! What is your hurry?"" I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I have recently gotten married."" He said, ""To a virgin or a previously married woman?"" I said, ""To a previously married woman."" He said, ""Why not a virgin, so you could play with her and she could play with you?"" Then, when we reached Madinah and were about to enter our homes, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Wait until night comes, i.e., until the time of 'Isha, so that the woman with disheveled hair may comb her hair, and the one whose husband has been away may shave her pubic hair."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""When you enter (your home), act wisely."" (That is, do not approach your wife if she is menstruating, and you have returned after many days and may not be able to restrain yourself.)"
